    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Histiocyte-predominant presentation of CD8+ T-cell&ndash;rich and granulomatous lesion in the setting of common variable immune deficiency",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Same patient shown in (&lt;&lt;32515&gt;&gt;, &lt;&lt;32520&gt;&gt;, &lt;&lt;32516&gt;&gt;) at 4&nbsp;years old, with worsening erythematous papules and red-brown plaques. A band-like, non-necrotizing confluent granulomatous infiltrate with minimal to absent lymphoid infiltrate is observed. The infiltrate is negative for S100, CD1a, and CD207 (langerin); positive for CD163, CD4, and CD68 (CD68 staining shown in &lt;&lt;32513&gt;&gt;); and negative for infectious etiologies after extensive workup.",
    "source": "Dita Gratzinger",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
